\p{Start a note suite on formulating theoretical intelligence potential, asking how much reliable capability post-training and agent procedures can obtain from a given pretrained model and how that depends on information, feedback, computation, and evaluation, kept comparative throughout: what improves, by which mechanism, at what cost, and on which tasks. It has since grown to close to nine hundred notes across post-training, agent systems, evaluation limits, and architecture, see [the notes](https://utensil.github.io/forest/ftip-0001/).}

